Prosody on FenrirOS
===================

Installed inert: the service is not enabled, there is no configuration, no
virtual host and no account. Upstream's example configuration (it enables
VirtualHost "localhost" and a commented example.com) is only
/usr/share/doc/prosody/prosody.cfg.lua.dist.

    cp /usr/share/doc/prosody/prosody.cfg.lua.dist /etc/prosody/prosody.cfg.lua
    chgrp prosody /etc/prosody/prosody.cfg.lua; chmod 640 /etc/prosody/prosody.cfg.lua
    $EDITOR /etc/prosody/prosody.cfg.lua   # your VirtualHost, certificates, admins
    prosodyctl check                        # validates the setup
    dinitctl enable prosody

Certificates go in /etc/prosody/certs (readable by the prosody group; a
Let's Encrypt setup can use `prosodyctl --root cert import`). Accounts:
`prosodyctl adduser user@host` (asks for the password). The service runs as the prosody user in the foreground (`prosody -F`; the
daemonize option is not used). Data is in /var/lib/prosody. The example
configuration logs to prosody.log and prosody.err in the working directory
(/var/lib/prosody); add `"*console"` to `log` to send logs to the service log
/var/log/prosody.log instead.

Community modules (mod_*) can be added under plugin_paths from
https://modules.prosody.im.
